//www.bluetooth.com/learn-about-bluetooth/feature-enhancements/direction-finding/`,un=`https://www.qorvo.com/resources/d/qorvo-getting-back-to-basics-with-ultra-wideband-uwb-white-paper`,dn=[{id:`ble-beacon`,name:`Bluetooth Beacon Positioning`,english:`BLUETOOTH BEACON`,tagline:`Build spatial visibility with lightweight deployment.`,description:`Start with practical questions: where is an asset, and is it inside the right zone? Low-power Bluetooth broadcasts connect people, assets and spaces while balancing installation cost, battery life and zone management.`,principle:`Beacons periodically broadcast an identifier. Fixed gateways can collect moving-tag broadcasts, or mobile terminals can scan fixed beacons. The platform estimates location using RSSI, zone rules or fingerprints. Choose the direction of deployment during system design.`,level:`Zone-level / meter-level positioning`,deployment:`Fixed gateways + mobile tags, or fixed beacons + scanning terminals`,scenarios:[`Asset inventory`,`Room-level management`,`Personnel zone counts`],steps:[{title:`Broadcast`,text:`Tags or beacons send identity and broadcast data.`},{title:`Collect and filter`,text:`Gateways or terminals scan and record signal strength.`},{title:`Estimate position`,text:`Use zone rules, RSSI or site fingerprints.`},{title:`Apply the data`,text:`Present asset zones, history and zone events.`}],benefits:[{title:`Incremental rollout`,text:`Start with key rooms, entrances or asset storage areas, then extend coverage.`},{title:`Flexible devices`,text:`Beacons, asset tags, badges and helmet terminals suit different objects.`},{title:`Adjustable policy`,text:`Tune broadcast intervals to motion, update and battery requirements.`}],considerations:[`People, shelving, walls and multipath affect RSSI. Sample the site and calibrate zone boundaries.`,`Radio coverage is not positioning accuracy. The JJ-IP32B specification lists a nominal 1–3m with a compatible gateway.`,`Confirm tag options and gateway downlink support for LEDs, buzzers, tamper alerts and bidirectional control.`],productIds:[`product-03`,`product-08`,`product-13`,`product-14`],reference:`https://www.bluetooth.com/blog/new-aoa-aod-bluetooth-capabilities/`,referenceName:`Bluetooth SIG · RSSI and direction finding`},{id:`ble-aoa`,name:`Bluetooth AoA Positioning`,english:`BLUETOOTH ANGLE OF ARRIVAL`,tagline:`Resolve direction to reveal a more precise location.`,description:`For medical equipment, production tools and personnel tracks that need finer location detail. Array gateways receive compatible tag signals and calculate position from angle observations and installation geometry.`,principle:`Compatible tags transmit direction-finding signals. A receiving antenna array collects phase information to estimate the angle of arrival. The engine combines gateway coordinates, orientation and target height or multiple observations to calculate position.`,level:`Sub-meter target; verify the model and site`,deployment:`AoA array gateways + compatible tags + positioning engine`,scenarios:[`Medical equipment`,`Tools and fixtures`,`Personnel tracks`],steps:[{title:`Transmit`,text:`Compatible tags send configured direction-finding signals.`},{title:`Measure angles`,text:`Array samples estimate azimuth and elevation.`},{title:`Calculate position`,text:`Combine station coordinates, orientation and height.`},{title:`Integrate`,text:`ACServer pushes results to the business system.`}],benefits:[{title:`Finer location detail`,text:`Direction information supports a transition from zones to coordinates.`},{title:`PoE installation`,text:`Ceiling mounting allows centralized network and power planning.`},{title:`Application interfaces`,text:`Connect through ACServer MQTT, HTTP or WebSocket interfaces.`}],considerations:[`Indoor JJ-IS40BXPA accuracy is specified as <0.5m unobstructed; the outdoor version specifies within 1m. Do not interchange these figures.`,`A coverage radius of about 1.5 times mounting height is nominal. Account for blind spots, target height and edge accuracy.`,`Standard iBeacon devices or a Bluetooth 5.x label alone do not establish AoA support. Verify direction-finding packets and firmware.`],productIds:[`product-12`,`product-11`,`product-06`,`product-18`],reference:ln,referenceName:`Bluetooth SIG · Direction Finding`},{id:`uwb-beacon`,name:`UWB Beacon Positioning`,english:`UWB BEACON ARCHITECTURE`,tagline:`Use precise timing to understand position.`,description:`Build a location system from UWB tags, reference stations and a positioning engine. Choose the ranging and calculation method around terminal count, battery demand and the available site network.`,principle:`UWB beacon describes a broadcast or reference-node role, not one specific algorithm. Systems may use two-way ranging (TWR), uplink TDoA or downlink reference broadcasts. Establish signal direction and synchronization requirements first.`,level:`Accuracy depends on the ranging mode and site`,deployment:`UWB tags + compatible stations + ranging / positioning engine`,scenarios:[`Production assets`,`Mobile tools`,`Logistics handling`],steps:[{title:`Choose architecture`,text:`Select broadcasts or two-way ranging and assign node roles.`},{title:`Observe signals`,text:`Receive timestamps or complete ranging exchanges.`},{title:`Solve position`,text:`Combine station coordinates and motion constraints.`},{title:`Connect operations`,text:`Associate location with equipment, work orders or goods.`}],benefits:[{title:`Detailed location targets`,text:`UWB time measurements suit applications with finer spatial requirements.`},{title:`Architecture options`,text:`Match the mode to tag count, update intervals and cabling.`},{title:`Dual-mode access`,text:`Bluetooth can handle configuration while UWB provides the selected ranging function.`}],considerations:[`UWB beacons do not use the Bluetooth iBeacon protocol. Their terminals and receiving paths are not interchangeable.`,`JJ-IP32BU is specified as reaching 0.3m with a compatible UWB gateway, channel and firmware combination.`,`Indoor gateway accuracy and frequency descriptions differ within the source. Validate a sample system before setting acceptance criteria.`],productIds:[`product-05`,`product-10`,`product-18`,`product-20`],reference:un,referenceName:`Qorvo · UWB fundamentals`},{id:`uwb-tdoa`,name:`UWB TDoA Positioning`,english:`TIME DIFFERENCE OF ARRIVAL`,tagline:`One broadcast. Multiple synchronized observations.`,description:`Uplink TDoA targets real-time systems with multiple tags. Stations record the arrival of a tag signal and use timing differences to constrain its position. Synchronization, geometry and capacity planning are central to the design.`,principle:`The same signal reaches different stations at different times. After synchronization or clock-offset correction, time differences become range differences. Multiple hyperbolic or hyperboloid constraints determine position.`,level:`Multi-tag coordinate tracking with system calibration`,deployment:`TDoA-compatible tags + synchronized station network + engine`,scenarios:[`Large warehouses`,`Production floors`,`Personnel and asset tracks`],steps:[{title:`Tag broadcast`,text:`Send scheduled UWB frames and control channel utilization.`},{title:`Multi-station reception`,text:`Capture the same frame and record its timestamps.`},{title:`Time-difference solution`,text:`Correct clocks and solve from arrival-time differences.`},{title:`Track output`,text:`Filter invalid observations and publish usable coordinates.`}],benefits:[{title:`Fewer tag exchanges`,text:`Uplink broadcasts reduce per-station two-way interactions for multi-tag systems.`},{title:`Central processing`,text:`Manage synchronization, observation quality and tracks through a common engine.`},{title:`Extendable coverage`,text:`Plan overlapping station coverage and suitable geometric placement.`}],considerations:[`Time synchronization is essential. Confirm its implementation and the timing error budget.`,`Station count depends on 2D/3D requirements, observability and redundancy; one fixed count cannot suit every deployment.`,`The supplied specifications do not provide a TDoA support list. Related UWB products are evaluation candidates only; verify timestamp and firmware capabilities first.`],productIds:[`product-10`,`product-05`],reference:un,referenceName:`Qorvo · UWB time-difference positioning`},{id:`uwb-pdoa`,name:`UWB PDoA Positioning`,english:`PHASE DIFFERENCE OF ARRIVAL`,tagline:`Use phase differences to understand direction.`,description:`For entry-direction detection, local guidance and combined range/angle applications. Phase differences across coherent receiving antennas estimate arrival direction; ranging or multiple stations provide the additional location constraints.`,principle:`A signal produces a phase difference at spatially separated antennas. Array geometry and RF calibration translate this into an angle estimate. An angle alone does not uniquely determine a complete position: range, additional angles or other constraints are normally required.`,level:`Angle / range fusion; confirm hardware capabilities`,deployment:`PDoA-capable RF hardware + calibrated array + compatible tags`,scenarios:[`Passage direction`,`Local target guidance`,`Range and angle fusion`],steps:[{title:`UWB signal`,text:`A compatible tag transmits a signal for phase observation.`},{title:`Coherent reception`,text:`Dedicated RF hardware obtains multi-antenna phase measurements.`},{title:`Calibrated angles`,text:`Calibrate phase, antennas and installation geometry.`},{title:`Constraint fusion`,text:`Combine range or multiple observations to determine position.`}],benefits:[{title:`Direction information`,text:`Add an angular dimension to support direction-aware applications.`},{title:`Local evaluation`,text:`Assess defined spaces such as entrances and workstations using sample hardware.`},{title:`Fusion options`,text:`Combine ranging, multiple stations and motion constraints as hardware permits.`}],considerations:[`PDoA requires suitable RF hardware. A UWB or dual-channel product name does not imply coherent phase measurements.`,`Antenna spacing, phase ambiguity, temperature drift and metal reflections affect angles; on-site calibration is required.`,`None of the supplied specifications explicitly confirms PDoA support. Related products are enquiry entry points, not a compatibility commitment.`],productIds:[`product-10`,`product-05`],reference:un,referenceName:`Qorvo · UWB phase differences and ranging`},{id:`tunnel`,name:`Tunnel & Utility Corridor Positioning`,english:`LINEAR SPACE POSITIONING`,tagline:`Keep location continuous along the work route.`,description:`Plan tunnel personnel tracking and asset location using one-dimensional chainage and section maps. Account for bends, branches and obstructions instead of applying a straight-line range claim to the entire tunnel.`,principle:`Dual-channel UWB stations and directional antennas observe corridor position, then map it to chainage and zones. The specification describes single-station 1D positioning; confirm ranging sequences and direction detection with compatible tags.`,level:`One-dimensional chainage positioning`,deployment:`Dual-channel stations + directional antennas + compatible terminals`,scenarios:[`Construction tunnels`,`Utility corridors`,`Metro sections`],steps:[{title:`Survey the route`,text:`Record chainage, bends, branches and construction obstructions.`},{title:`Place stations`,text:`Install antennas, stations, PoE and backhaul.`},{title:`Calibrate sections`,text:`Validate location, handovers and coverage boundaries.`},{title:`Connect operations`,text:`Use chainage for personnel counts and zone-event applications.`}],benefits:[{title:`Fit linear spaces`,text:`Chainage and section identifiers suit construction and inspection workflows.`},{title:`Installation-ready hardware`,text:`JJ-U provides an IP67 cast-aluminum station with antennas and brackets.`},{title:`Central maintenance`,text:`PoE carries data and power; mini program or AC tools manage configuration.`}],considerations:[`JJ-U nominal ranging accuracy is 30cm and the 400m transmission figure assumes line of sight. Bends and vehicles may require additional coverage.`,`Single-station 1D support is not unrestricted 2D/3D positioning. Branches need suitable maps and deployment planning.`,`Match tag channels and protocols. Select equipment for hazardous areas using its actual certificates and project requirements.`],productIds:[`product-17`,`product-18`],reference:un,referenceName:`Qorvo · UWB ranging fundamentals`},{id:`hybrid`,name:`Indoor–Outdoor Hybrid Positioning`,english:`HYBRID LOCATION & CONNECTIVITY`,tagline:`Cross building boundaries with a connected view.`,description:`Use Bluetooth or AoA indoors, GPS/BeiDou outdoors where supported, and LoRa or 4G for backhaul. A common object identity associates different location sources as people and assets move between buildings.`,principle:`The terminal or platform selects valid location sources using timestamps and quality, then aggregates data over LoRa, Ethernet or cellular links. Backhaul transports data; accuracy still depends on the positioning technology and environment.`,level:`Multiple location sources`,deployment:`Multi-mode terminals + indoor gateways + outdoor backhaul`,scenarios:[`Industrial campuses`,`Cross-building assets`,`Personnel inspections`],steps:[{title:`Unify identity`,text:`Associate terminals with personnel and asset records.`},{title:`Position by zone`,text:`Use BLE/AoA indoors and configured satellite positioning outdoors.`},{title:`Aggregate data`,text:`Forward status and position through LoRa, Ethernet or 4G.`},{title:`Fuse sources`,text:`Track source, time and quality to manage transitions.`}],benefits:[{title:`Choose by area`,text:`Plan accuracy targets and networks for each operating environment.`},{title:`One object view`,text:`Associate personnel and assets across indoor and outdoor workflows.`},{title:`Suitable form factors`,text:`Badges, e-paper devices, helmet terminals and asset tags suit different field uses.`}],considerations:[`LoRa and LoRaWAN require compatible protocols, bands and gateways. Frequency alone does not establish interoperability.`,`Source switching, buffering and fusion must be designed and tested during platform integration, not assumed to be standard hardware functions.`,`UWB, BeiDou, AIS, 4G and access control are model options. Confirm device combinations and battery policy first.`],productIds:[`product-18`,`product-16`,`product-04`,`product-19`,`product-15`,`product-07`],reference:ln,referenceName:`Bluetooth SIG · Indoor direction finding`}],fn=()=>(0,k.jsxs)(k.Fragment,{children:[(0,k.jsx)(tn,{}),(0,k.jsx)(nn,{}),(0,k.jsxs)(`section`,{className:`site-container pt-10 sm:pt-14 md:pt-16 lg:pt-20`,children:[(0,k.jsx)(rn,{eyebrow:`OUR HARDWARE / HARDWARE`,title:`Every node of your positioning network`,description:`Positioning stations, connectivity gateways and versatile terminals for different accuracy and coverage needs.`,children:(0,k.jsxs)(`a`,{href:`./products/`,className:`secondary-button shrink-0`,children:[`All products`,(0,k.jsx)(w,{size:16})]})}),(0,k.jsx)(`div`,{className:`grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 md:gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3`,children:[`product-12`,`product-17`,`product-05`].map(e=>cn.find(t=>t.id===e)).filter(e=>e!==void 0).map(e=>(0,k.jsx)(on,{product:e},e.id))})]}),(0,k.jsxs)(`section`,{className:`site-container pt-16 sm:pt-20 md:pt-24 lg:pt-28`,children:[(0,k.jsx)(rn,{eyebrow:`BUILT AROUND YOUR SCENARIO / Solutions`,title:`Choose technology around your application.`,description:`Explore zone detection, direction finding and UWB positioning to match the conditions on your site.`,children:(0,k.jsxs)(`a`,{href:`./solutions/`,className:`secondary-button shrink-0`,children:[`All solutions`,(0,k.jsx)(w,{size:16})]})}),(0,k.jsx)(`div`,{className:`grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 md:gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3`,children:dn.slice(0,6).map(e=>(0,k.jsx)(sn,{